WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.400
In the year 383, Fu Jian led a great army south, said to number a million men.

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:15.350
The Eastern Jin had only eighty thousand men, yet their commander Xie An stayed perfectly calm — he was still playing chess.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:21.124
When his friend asked whether he was afraid, he only smiled slightly and went on placing his pieces.

00:00:21.474 --> 00:00:26.466
The two armies faced each other across the Fei River, and a great battle was about to begin.

00:00:26.816 --> 00:00:33.128
The river flowed quietly on, and the soldiers on both banks held their breath.

00:00:33.478 --> 00:00:37.774
The Eastern Jin army seized the moment, crossed the river, and launched its attack on the Former Qin.

00:00:38.124 --> 00:00:43.284
The Former Qin ranks fell into great disorder, and the soldiers fell back one after another.

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:49.466
When the victory report arrived, Xie An was still playing chess — he did not even raise his head.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:54.808
Only after the guests left did he leap up with joy — he even broke his wooden clogs.

00:00:55.158 --> 00:01:00.990
At the Battle of Fei River, the Eastern Jin defeated the many with the few, creating a miracle in history.

